<!--
    Status-bar / lock-screen media-notification icon (audio_service's
    androidNotificationIcon: 'drawable/ic_notification'). Android always
    renders this as a flat white silhouette regardless of the fillColor
    used here (SDK re-tints status-bar icons to white/monochrome from
    API 21 on), so white is used directly rather than the brand gold.

    Sizing: the previous ic_notification.png filled ~47% of its 72px
    (24dp @ xxhdpi) canvas (34px content / 72px canvas). A first pass
    scaled this vector to ~61% fill (scaleX/Y 0.89025 applied to the
    raw path, whose own bounding box already fills ~69% of the 1024
    viewport). Still read as noticeably smaller than other apps'
    media notification/lock-screen icons, so bumped to scaleX/Y 1.05
    (~72% fill). Bumped again by +12.5% to scaleX/Y 1.18125 (1.05 *
    1.125) — ~81% fill on the tall axis, ~70% on the wide axis. The
    path's own bbox is taller than it is wide (705 x 608 of the 1024
    viewport), so the tall axis is the binding constraint and clips
    against the viewport edge past scaleX/Y ~1.45. translateX/Y
    recenter the path's own bounding-box pivot to the 1024 canvas
    center and don't need to change with the scale, since scaling
    happens around that same pivot.
-->
